  <section class="summary" aria-labelledby="sum">
    <h2 id="sum">The 30 second version</h2>
    <div><span class="k">Problem</span><p>Seven in ten orders hold a single product, even though the bottle and bag come in the same print.</p></div>
    <div><span class="k">Decision</span><p>The obvious second product is not whatever a recommendation engine guesses. It is the same character in the next thing on the school checklist.</p></div>
    <div><span class="k">The one metric that matters</span><p>Share of orders with 2 or more items, starting from 30%.</p></div>
    <div><span class="k">What I learned</span><p>Before designing a new discount, check whether the one already being paid for is visible at the moment of decision. Here the fix was placement and framing, not money.</p></div>
  </section>

